    "path": "profiles/contributed_custom_profiles.go",
    "date": "2026-11-03",
    "note": "Transcribed, not captured: the TLS ClientHello (cipher suites and extensions with their parameters, in tls-client's order) and the HTTP/2 SETTINGS, window increment, pseudo-header order and priority are tls-client's MeshAndroid. Everything else stands on the captured okhttp-5.5-conscrypt: OkHttp's header set (OkHttp, measured over HTTP/2 only, has no HTTP/1.1 set). An app sends its own User-Agent and headers, which tls-client does not describe: set them on the session. Kept as tls-client has it: its ALPS extension names no protocol (BoringSSL sends ALPS only with one)."
